264-## 6. API surface & SSE event shape (frozen)
265-
266:Routes exactly as the spec lists (`/api/workflows` CRUD+import/export; `/api/workflow/node-types|validate|run|executions/*`). New blueprint `workflows_bp`, name `"workflows"`, **no url_prefix** (matches all 14 existing blueprints), imported and registered with the other blueprints in `app.py`. Provider-backed option resolution occurs at request time after startup initialization; blueprint registration itself must not assume populated provider registries.
267-
268-All endpoints are local-app endpoints and enforce `is_loopback_remote`; mutation endpoints also
269-require JSON content types where applicable. Success payloads are JSON objects rather than bare
270-arrays. Errors use one envelope everywhere:
--
288-| `GET /api/workflows/<id>` | — | `200 {workflow}`; `404` if absent |
289-| `PUT /api/workflows/<id>` | `{workflow, expected_updated_at}` | `200 {workflow}`; `409 WORKFLOW_CONFLICT` on stale update |
290-| `DELETE /api/workflows/<id>` | `{expected_updated_at?}` | `200 {deleted:true, workflow_id}` after atomic move to trash; `409` on stale update |
291-| `POST /api/workflows/import` | `{workflow, on_conflict:"reject"|"new_id"}` | `201 {workflow, imported_from_id?}`; default `new_id` |
292:| `GET /api/workflows/<id>/export` | — | `200 application/json` definition with attachment filename; no execution data/secrets |
293-| `GET /api/workflow/node-types` | — | `200 {registry_version, node_types, port_types}` with no executor/callable internals |
294-| `GET /api/workflow/templates` | — | `200 {templates:[{template_id, workflow}]}`; every bundled graph passes server validation |
295-| `POST /api/workflow/validate` | `{workflow}` | `200 {valid, problems, warnings}` for a well-formed request, even when graph-invalid; malformed transport is `400` |
296:| `POST /api/workflow/run` | `{workflow_id xor workflow, run_mode, target_node_ids:[], force:false, project_id?}` | `202 {execution_id, project_id, status:"queued"}` |
297:| `POST /api/workflow/executions/<id>/stop` | `{}` | `202 {execution_id, status:"cancelling"}`; `409` if already terminal |
298:| `GET /api/workflow/executions/<id>` | — | `200 {execution}`; `404` if absent |
299:| `GET /api/workflow/executions/<id>/events` | standard `Last-Event-ID` on reconnect | `200 text/event-stream`; `404` if absent |
300:| `GET /api/workflow/executions` | required `workflow_id`, optional `limit` 1–200 | `200 {executions:[summary], total:n}` sorted newest first |
301-
302-Create/import/save return `422 WORKFLOW_INVALID` when the JSON transport is valid but violates
303-workflow rules. Use `400` for malformed JSON/request shape, `403` for non-loopback access,
304-`404` for missing resources, `409` for conflicts/locks/terminal stop, `413` for size limits,
--
307-
308-SSE (own emitter in `studio/workflows/events.py` — do NOT reuse pipeline `_emit`, which is private and closes over `_jobs`; see blocker B6):
309-
310-```jsonc
311:{ "sequence": 12, "execution_id": "ex_123", "node_id": "n_tts",
312-  "status": "running", "attempt": 1, "timestamp": "ISO",
313-  "duration_ms": 0, "summary": "Generating narration",
314-  "progress": {"ready": 3, "total": 10},      // optional, poll-driven nodes
315:  "from_sample_data": false }                  // present when stub-fed
316-```
317:Monotonic `sequence` per execution; each SSE frame includes `id: <sequence>` and a JSON `data:` payload. The stream ends on terminal event `{node_id: null, status: "succeeded|failed|cancelled"}`. On automatic reconnect, browser `EventSource` sends the standard `Last-Event-ID` header; the server replays events with greater sequence values from a bounded ring (1000 events). If the requested ID predates the retained buffer, emit a snapshot/reset event before live events. The client also deduplicates by `sequence`.
